Design a pipelined Johnson counter with a 64-bit shift register that generates a 4-bit output. On each clock cycle, the counter shifts its bits to the left and incorporates feedback from specific bits in the shift register to create a unique sequence. The output, Q, comprises the four most significant bits of the shift register. The counter is reset asynchronously, clearing the shift register and output when the reset signal is low.
