description:
Design an 8-bit Linear Feedback Shift Register (LFSR) that generates pseudo-random sequences. The output (`out`) is initialized to `4'b1111` upon reset. On each positive clock edge, when enabled, the LFSR shifts its bits left while introducing new bits derived from selected XOR operations on specific bits of the current output. This configuration allows for the generation of unique and varied output patterns, useful in applications such as digital communication and cryptography.
