description:
Design a debouncer circuit for a digital input signal. The module takes a potentially noisy input and filters it to produce a stable output. It does this by counting clock cycles during which the input signal remains unchanged. When the input transitions, a counter resets, and once the counter reaches a predetermined debounce time, the output is updated to reflect the stable state of the input. This ensures that brief fluctuations in the input signal do not cause erroneous changes in the output, effectively eliminating bounce and providing a clean signal for further processing.
module top_module(
  input wire clk, // Added clk input
  input wire in,
  output reg out
);

